  info: 'Mosquitos, meaning little flies in Spanish, are a species belonging to the
    order Diptera known for drinking blood. Only females of certain mosquito species
    can drink blood, but all species of mosquito can drink nectar using their piercing-sucking
    mouthparts. Mosquitos are also known to be vectors of disease such as Malaria
    and Yellow fever.


    Source: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mosquito '
